.\" strip.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX strip(1) utility, which
.\" this tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/STRIP.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/STRIP.
.TH STRIP 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
strip \- remove unnecessary information from executable files
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Strip
is not provided on maux.
maux's binaries are flat, headerless images with no symbol table
embedded in them at all, so there is nothing for strip to
remove.
